<Project>
  <!--
    The entry-point list. The source generator writes the names of every [CleatEntry] method to
    $(CleatEntryPointsFile) as it generates the dispatch table, so the list and the table come from one pass and
    cannot disagree. The csharp target of `cleat build` reads the file into cleat.metadata.entry_points
    (cleat#4080).

    Why the generator writes it: a build task that read the compiled assembly's metadata was tried first and
    dropped. The inline-task compiler does not reference System.Reflection.Metadata, and no consistent set of
    references made it compile (the runtime's implementation assemblies and the reference pack each lost
    System.Object). A generator already holds the names, and the path reaches it as a compiler-visible property.

    The default is obj/cleat-entry-points.txt: BaseIntermediateOutputPath, because IntermediateOutputPath is not
    defined yet where a project imports this file, and the path should not depend on configuration or runtime anyway.
    Ask MSBuild for the path rather than rebuilding it from the layout:
        dotnet msbuild -getProperty:CleatEntryPointsFile
    Format: UTF-8 without a BOM, LF line endings, one entry name per line, in the compiler's declaration order,
    no blank lines, a final newline. A name never contains a comma or a line break (the generator refuses one), so
    the file can be split on lines or joined with commas without ambiguity.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <CleatEntryPointsFile Condition="'$(CleatEntryPointsFile)' == ''">$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/$(BaseIntermediateOutputPath)cleat-entry-points.txt</CleatEntryPointsFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="CleatEntryPointsFile" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The file is written when the compiler runs the generator. If the compiler was skipped as up to date and the
       file has since been deleted, there is nothing to read, and the failure should name the cause. -->
  <Target Name="CleatCheckEntryPoints" AfterTargets="CoreCompile">
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(CleatEntryPointsFile)')"
           Text="cleat: $(CleatEntryPointsFile) was not written. The generator writes it while compiling; rebuild with --no-incremental." />
  </Target>
</Project>
